From 73bcd4c8f835326e8e8a276b291bb19c111acc9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:56:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 091/114] HACK: power: qcom_battmgr: OnePlus charging policy
 for USB-C PD

The OnePlus charger firmware leaves all charging policy to the AP, which
Android keeps in oplus_chg: VBUS stays at 5 V and battery current at
500 mA unless told otherwise, and the firmware cannot see the temperature
of the battery, since the gauge sits on an AP I2C bus.

Add that policy, enabled by the new oplus,fuel-gauge DT property:
- PD chargers: ask for 9 V once the partner's SVID is known (or after
  three polls), with an input limit of 2 A or what the charger offers.
- DCP and 5 V PD: climb the input limit to 2 A, CDP to 1.5 A, backing off
  if VBUS sags under 4.4 V. SDP stays at the firmware's 500 mA.
- Battery current and float voltage by gauge temperature, from the vendor
  DT limits: no charging under 0 C or over 50 C, 600 mA/8.24 V from 47 C,
  3 A at 16-47 C (1.1 A on 5 V). The firmware's lower 8.7 V float voltage
  stays, instead of the vendor's 8.87 V, for the worn battery.
- Stop at full (under 150 mA near the float voltage: the gauge expects a
  higher one, so doesn't report full), recharge below 8.5 V.
- Stay awake while charging, as nothing watches temperature in suspend.

Report the adapter type in usb_type: the firmware's USB_TYPE stays at the
BC1.2 result even on PD. Add a raw bat_prop debugfs next to usb_prop.

Tested with a PD charger: 8.84 V at the phone, 2.77 A offered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
